## 3.2. Active NPs Surrounded by MOFs
The “bottle-around-ship” approach is widely used for achieving effective encapsulation of active NPs by porous MOFs.  Generally, this strategy involves two steps.  First, active NPs with well-defined structures are synthesized. Second, the active NPs are introduced into the precursor solution of an MOF to form the encapsulation structures. Therefore, the key to acquire the well-defined structure is to avoid aggregation of active NPs and self-nucleation of MOF shells.  For example, Kitagawa et al.
## 3.2.1. Bridging Active NP Core and MOF Shell by Surfactant/Ligand Molecules
